any part of it.

Until 2026-09-13 the project shipped under GPL-3.0, because two seamless-tiling
shaders (`seamlessMaker` and `seamlessSplat`) had been ported from Materialize
(BoundingBoxSoftware, GPL-3.0). Both were removed — from the live tool and from
the archived v1 copy — and replaced with independent implementations of published
techniques:

  * multi-band (Laplacian pyramid) edge blending — Burt & Adelson 1983; GPU
    formulation per "GPU-Friendly Laplacian Texture Blending", JCGT 14(1), 2025
  * variance-preserving ("histogram-preserving") stamp blending — Heitz & Neyret,
    High-Performance Graphics 2018

No Materialize code remains anywhere in this repository, including in
`Archive/TextureTool-v1/`. The archived v1 tool was ported to the same MIT
replacements rather than being left GPL-3.0; its README records that it is
therefore not a byte-for-byte historical copy, and points at git for the
unmodified original.

Third-party components bundled or loaded at runtime keep their own licenses; see
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. All of them are permissive (MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD).

